---
title: "create_and_share_price_feeds_using_verified_price_infos (Pyth Sui Contracts)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_loop: !vector::is_empty(price_infos)
    q_loop --> q_pop: true
    q_loop --> [*]: false, return
    q_pop --> q_exists: cur_price_info = pop_back(price_infos)
    q_exists --> q_loop: price_feed_object_exists == true (skip)
    q_exists --> q_create: price_feed_object_exists == false
    q_create --> q_new_obj: new_price_info_object(cur_price_info, ctx)
    q_new_obj --> q_register: state::register_price_info_object(latest_only, pyth_state, id)
    q_register --> q_share: transfer::public_share_object(new_price_info_object)
    q_share --> q_loop

    note right of q_exists
        INV-001: price feed objects are only created once per price_identifier
        INV-002: new objects are registered in state AND shared publicly
        INV-003: duplicate price identifiers are silently skipped
    end note
